# Tracking — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/tracking.sops.json.

# BookStack
# A MISSING value makes the init script `sleep infinity` — the container
# reports running forever and only /status catches it. It must decode to
# EXACTLY 32 bytes (Laravel AES-256-CBC): a 33-byte value boots, migrates and
# serves, then throws "Unsupported cipher or incorrect key length" during
# middleware termination, after the response, with nothing in the log.
#   docker run --rm --entrypoint /bin/bash \
#     lscr.io/linuxserver/bookstack:version-v26.05.4 appkey
APP_KEY=changeme_base64_32_raw_bytes
# Applied from inside the container by bookstack-admin-init.sh, replacing the
# seeded admin@admin.com / password account — it refuses a placeholder, which
# leaves that seeded account live. A break-glass LOCAL admin: its email must
# not be an Authentik user's — SSO already owns idan@idanreed.com, and
# create-admin refuses an address in use, leaving the seeded account live.
BOOKSTACK_ADMIN_EMAIL=bookstack-admin@idanreed.com
BOOKSTACK_ADMIN_NAME=Idan
BOOKSTACK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme_strong_password

# MariaDB
# MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD keeps that exact spelling (not MARIADB_) because
# nixos/backup-prepare.sh reads it from the container env for mysqldump.
# MARIADB_PASSWORD and DB_PASSWORD hold the same app-user value.
# openssl rand -hex 24
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=changeme_hex24
MARIADB_PASSWORD=changeme_hex24

# Homebox
# REQUIRED AT STARTUP and >= 32 bytes — absent from nearly every compose
# example online, so a copied config just refuses to start. NEVER ROTATE: it
# invalidates every API key ever issued. openssl rand -base64 48
HBOX_AUTH_API_KEY_PEPPER=changeme_base64_48
HOMEBOX_ADMIN_EMAIL=idan@idanreed.com
HOMEBOX_ADMIN_NAME=Idan
HOMEBOX_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme_strong_password

# Karakeep
# NEVER ROTATE NEXTAUTH_SECRET once sessions exist — it signs both sessions and
# asset URLs. openssl rand -base64 36
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=changeme_base64_36
# Read by BOTH karakeep and meilisearch, which refuses to start in production
# without >= 16 bytes. openssl rand -base64 32
MEILI_MASTER_KEY=changeme_base64_32
KARAKEEP_ADMIN_EMAIL=idan@idanreed.com
KARAKEEP_ADMIN_NAME=Idan
KARAKEEP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme_strong_password

